1218 0 obj
<<
/Title (Project Overview: This project was coded in MATLAB and integrated with NASA's Chemical Equilibrium with Applications in MATLAB \(CEAM\) software to compute combustion thermodynamic data. This algorithm takes user-defined geometry ranges \(throat/exit radii, expansion ratios\), ideal thrust, chamber scale, and gas reservoir parameters. It evaluates 2,000+ geometries via 1-dimensional isentropic flow analysis, filters down to a single optimal nozzle, prints flow results to the MATLAB terminal, generates three figures \(nozzle optimization, flow profiles, and transient performance\), and exports geometry data for ANSYS Fluent. Next, I will validate the performance metrics in a 2D ANSYS Fluent flow simulation using matching parameters.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 884 0 R
/Next 1315 0 R
>>
endobj
